Read inherited options and top index in list-widget appearances (MuPDF 1.28.5)

This file modifies MuPDF. The Mervin PDF project added this local fix on
2026-10-23. It is not an upstream backport. Remove it when the pinned MuPDF
release reads these entries from the field hierarchy when regenerating list
widget appearances.

A choice field can keep its option array and top index on a parent shared by
widgets on multiple pages. MuPDF's choice enumeration already inherits /Opt,
but its list appearance writer reads /Opt and /TI only from the widget. Editing
a valid shared list field can therefore replace its stored appearance with a
blank one. Use the existing inherited dictionary accessors, as the other field
attributes do. Do not copy field entries to the widgets or change the list to a
combo box.

This patch restores rendered option text and the authored top index. It does
not implement the existing TODO for highlighting selected list items. /V and
selection semantics remain independent of that upstream rendering limitation.

diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c b/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
@@ -2895,8 +2895,8 @@ pdf_write_ch_widget_appearance(fz_context *ctx, pdf_annot *annot, fz_buffer *buf,
 		fz_buffer *text = fz_new_buffer(ctx, 1024);
 		fz_try(ctx)
 		{
-			pdf_obj *opt = pdf_dict_get(ctx, annot->obj, PDF_NAME(Opt));
-			int i = pdf_dict_get_int(ctx, annot->obj, PDF_NAME(TI));
+			pdf_obj *opt = pdf_dict_get_inheritable(ctx, annot->obj, PDF_NAME(Opt));
+			int i = pdf_dict_get_inheritable_int(ctx, annot->obj, PDF_NAME(TI));
 			int n = pdf_array_len(ctx, opt);
 			/* TODO: Scrollbar */
 			/* TODO: Highlight selected items */
